I know I don't post here much (my last game report was in 2006, last
post of any kind in March of this year) but I've been lurking here the
whole time.  But, I managed to ascend last night for the first time.
This comes after about 2 1/2 years of playing Nethack.  (But 20+ of
playing Roguelikes in general.  I was a Moria player starting circa
1987.  I never won Moria, for the record.)

Anyway, this particular game was played online at NAO.  It started in
mid April of this year.  (Keep in mind there was a gap in June, July
and early August where I didn't play it, so it wasn't 6 months of non
stop playing.)  More significantly than that, I was virtually
unspoiled until I got to dlvl 35 or so.  (Hanging around here, you
can't help but pick up a few spoilers.)  At 35, I thought to myself,
"I have to win this.  The only way I can ensure that is by checking
spoilers as needed.")  I tried not to get excessive, but I definitely
read up on end game strategy.

As for the game itself:

I lost my pet on dlvl 1 to a fire trap (that would have certainly
killed me as well if I had stepped on it.)  The early game was mostly
unremarkable and standard Barbarian stuff.  Get Cleaver, fight through
the hordes with Cleaver.  After clearing the Mines out, I decided to
do some Altar camping and ending up being granted Stormbringer, which
I used for the rest of the game.  (#twoweaponing with a silver saber
from mid game on.)  Found a bag of holding early on (I think on dlvl 4
or 5, actually) and was happy to do Sokoban and get the Amulet of
Reflection.

Around this time, I made a failed attempt at polypiling.  The best
thing I got was a Bag of Holding, which I didn't need.  Unicorns were
plentiful in this game and, if I hadn't polypiled horns, I probably
would have had at least 10 in my stash.  (In addition to the three I
carried with me.)

I hit 14 and did my Quest.  This marks the first game where I even
made it to a high enough level to do my Quest.  It's very weird in
that I could never make it very far at all (with dlvl 11 being
considered quite good) and then suddenly I ascend.

Continuing on, I made it safely to Medusa, got the version without the
Titan.  And, in fact, if you look at my dumplog, you'll see I did not
encounter a Titan at all during the game.  Briefly considered adding
Perseus' shield and giving up #twoweaponing.  (I was using a long
sword at this point.)  Decided against it.

For most this game, I had a declining AC problem.  My armor kept
getting destroyed and I ended up fighting through the Castle with an
AC of just -12.  (As high as -17 earlier in the game.)  I lost 2 suits
of Elvish Mithril and a very nice +2 Cloak of Displacement, in
addition to several helmets.  Polymorph traps were responsible for a
lot of that.  When I finally made the Castle and got the Wand, I
rectified that.  Magic Marker was the first wish and I wrote up some
useful scrolls.  (Including Charging.)  I killed a silver dragon and
made SDSM that way, rather than wishing for it.  (This after a lengthy
discussion with friends over why I should be using SDSM instead of
GDSM.)  My ascension gear was rounded out with an Amulet of Life
Saving (I was terrified of going below the castle without one.  As it
turns out, I didn't need it.), Speed Boots, Gauntlets of Power, Cloak
of MR and a Hawaiian Shirt enchanted to +5.  I wished for all of this
except the Shirt.  After writing up multiple scrolls to enchant my new
gear, I continued on.

I fought down through the mazes below the castle and wound up at
Vlad's Tower.  Killed him in a remarkably quick fashion.  (I think it
took 3 hits.) and took all his goodies.  (Including a second Amulet of
Lifesaving.)  I fought down further, again with nothing remarkable
happening, until I got to the bottom level and routed out the
vibrating square.  I dropped a credit card on it.

By this point, I was pretty much in "I'm gonna make it!" ascension
mode.  I had the above mentioned armor on, about 8 wands of digging
for Earth, a couple wands of teleport (for clearing out crowds in
Astral), tons of scrolls and potions for any possible circumstance,
multiple unicorn horns.  At this point I travelled back to the Castle
(where I kept my wand of wishing) and wrested the final wish out of my
wand.  In my earlier ignorance, I had burned all of Izchak's candles
exploring the Mine.  That was dumb of me.  I wished for 7 blessed
candles.  I sat on the Throne and got a genocide, so I genocided Mind
Flayers.  (I had genocided Liches earlier after writing up a Genocide
scroll.)  I sat on the Throne again and got another wish and I
actually don't remember what I wished for.  I think some kind of
armor.

So, anyway, at this point I travelled down to the start of Rodney's
tower and then stopped playing for 3 weeks due to personal issues that
left me little time for Nethack.   I picked it up again last night.
After forgetting how to get into Rodney's Tower and asking for help on
#nethack, I continued on.  I blasted my way through everyone there.
Gave Rodeny a quick zap with Orcus' Death Wand and grabbed the Book of
the Dead.  (I always imagined this to be the Necronomicon from HP
Lovecraft's works, but I don't think it's intended to be that.)  Not
knowing how often Rodney would come back to annoy me (I was imagining
every 100 turns or so, to be honest.) I ran like hell to the Vibrating
Square and performed the invocation ritual... and surrounded myself
with undead.  I fought them off and wondered what the hell had gone
wrong.  I had done everything correctly.  Lit the candelabrum, rang
the bell, read the book.  I did the exact same thing again and it
worked this time.  Moloch's graveyard gave me a bit of trouble, but I
did end up finding a Wraith corpse and ate that, another level never
hurts.

Let me take a moment out to assure everyone here... the game is SO
MUCH EASIER with a Ring of Conflict.  There's no way I would have
survived in certain parts of the game without that ring.  Most of you
probably know it already, but I thought I'd mention it anyway.  I
mention it now because it made the graveyard much easier.  This is one
item I will be wishing for in the future if I don't find one.

Anyway, back to the game.  Moloch's Priest went down easily, I was
surprised to find.  Almost as easily as Vlad.  I grabbed the Amulet of
Yendor and ran like hell.  I stopped for nothing, I slaughtered
anything (including friendlies) in my way.  Well, one correction.  I
did stop at a co-aligned altar and #prayed for the final time on it.
I got a free point of divine protection.  I imagined myself saying,
"Thanks Set!  *holds up the Amulet* This is gonna be yours in a
minute!"

I blew past my dlvl 14 stash (not nearly deep enough, for the
record).  Just above it, there's an altar (wrong alignment) with a
Priest and peaceful Elf in it.  I BUC id-ed so many things there, I
sort of felt like I was friends with the Priest and the Elf.  I could
imagine them saying, "Why are you in such a hurry?" to me as I flew
by.  I held out the Amulet as I ran by saying, "Rodney is after me!
Gotta get to the Astral Plane!"  After I left, The Elf would turn to
the Priest and say, "Shouldn't've you have killed him?  Doesn't your
God want that Amulet too?"  The Priest would mumble a response and
tell the Elf to shut up.

Truth be told, I was sort of sad to leave this particular set of
dungeons behind.  I knew the entire dungeon very well thanks to
running up and down it so much.  Even when I got to dlvls 1-5 (which I
never returned to after leaving), it almost felt Deja Vu-like.  I
stopped for just a moment at the fire trap that killed my cat so long
ago.  I dedicated my forth coming ascension (I still wasn't sure I
would, though) to my cat, who had saved my life earlier in the game by
letting me know where the fire trap was, a spot I would have likely
stepped on because it was close to the stairs.

Rodney mad his reappearance in Earth, and I just zapped him with the
Death wand.  He had hassled me earlier on when I got to Juiblex' lair,
and I took him out by fighting him normally.  I had made a tactical
error here, though, and had come into the Planes without a method of
detecting portals.  This was frustrating.  I got lucky and found the
Earth portal quickly.  Air made me want to scream, as it took me
probably half an hour to find the portal.  (I ended up just walking
over every square to the right of the cloud banks until I found it.)
I got lucky again in Fire and found the portal after about 50 turns.
(I realized there was no set place for the portal to be, so I decided
I'd have to walk over every square.   I started walking on the bottom
most row of the plane, and that's the row the portal happened to be
on.)  Water was nearly as bad as Air, and I spent 10 minutes going
between bubbles.

So, up next was Astral.  All the portals seemed about equally far
away, so I decided to take the one with Famine by it.  I had 15
rations and 3 lumps of royal jelly.  He should pose little threat.  He
went down easily, ring of conflict went on, and I teleported the crowd
out of my way.  Neutral altar.  Crud.  Getting out wasn't so easy.
For some reason, I took the ring off and got trapped between Famine
and some angels.  I was down to 64hp at one point and blind, stunned
and hungry.  I was thinking it was a good thing I had that Amulet.
However, I pulled out a potion of full healing, drank that, and then
put the ring on.  Killed Famine on the way out and then decided to hit
up the middle altar.

Just getting out took me down to 170hp, so I hung around near where I
came in, killed a few insects that were summoned and continued on.
Death greeted me as I opened the door to the chamber and, honestly, he
went down faster than Vlad.  I killed someone in my way (someone
named.  Bill the Heretic or something.) and ran right to the altar.
Apparently, having the Ring of Conflict on from the start helps with
bottlenecking.  IDed it.  Set!  Chaotic! It's time!

But then my connection to NAO dropped.  What the hell?  Please,
please, please don't let NAO have gone down.  I reconnected and
apparently my DSL just had a problem.

I go back in, re-identify the altar once more to be positive and then
#offer

DYWYPI?

Hell yes!

Since this game was played on NAO, the dumplog is online at
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/AstroSteve/dumplog/1208134264.nh343.txt

I will also copy and paste it here as well.  Let me just say, this was
an epic game of Nethack.  100,000 turns (almost) and one of m friends
says he's never seen an alignment higher than mine, 507. (though I
wasn't going for that.)

Next up?  A Wizard!

